{
  "_doc": "The castle's far silhouette (docs/architecture.md, docs/art/castle-kit.md 'Exterior'). The HLOD chunks are made from it (tools/blender/world/hlod_export.py): a chunk with `cells` stands in for those playable cells (their outer walls and roofs from the layout, at low detail, set 0.3 m inside the real walls) and hides while all of them are loaded; a chunk with no `cells` is exterior-only massing (towers and ranges with no interior yet, roof caps over playable towers) and is drawn whenever the viewer stands outdoors. Every playable castle cell is in exactly one chunk, or in `no_outside` (below ground or inside other cells: nothing of it shows from outside). `masses` are the exterior-only shapes, placed to read as a crowded Gothic skyline of towers, spires and steep roofs from the grounds and the lake around our playable layout: `box` (min/max [x, z]) or `round` (centre [x, z], radius; drawn as a 12-sided drum) from `base` to `top` (y, metres); `roof`: `cone` (a round or square spire of `roof_height`), `pyramid`, `pitched` (ridge along `ridge`, `roof_height` above the eaves), `flat` (a crenellated parapet, 1.5 m). `rise` (caps only, optional): a turret's walls this high over the cell's roof before its roof (a round cap with `rise` reads as a round tower top). `over` (caps only): a playable cell whose highest roof the cap stands on (its base comes from the layout). Stone: one outside stone, the west range's pale cool `castle_wall_c` (its `@ext` clone) on every outside face; roofs `castle_roof`; windows as darker bands in the greyscale COLOR_0 (`windows`: true). No colour is written here. More vertical variety (taller and slimmer spires, a few squat ones, five new slender turrets), `steep_roofs`: a cell's facade roof redrawn steeper over the real one (from its eaves, `pitch` degrees; the Great Hall's long steep roof, in an exterior-only chunk so it shows whether or not the cell is loaded), and `crag`: the rock faces under the outer walls on the lake side and round the north (world/hlod_crag.py), each run a line along the walls' foot (`inner`, outside every playable space and off the grounds' box) with the rock thrown to `side` out to its cliff edge (`rim` m) and its foot (`foot` m; under `water` when given, else under the ground), on `material` (the palette's `colour`). Stable courtyard walls (2026-11): a mass stops at least 0.3 m (grid.P3A_HLOD_INSET) behind any playable cell's wall it backs onto, never flush with it: a flush face z-fights with the real wall (the Clock Tower ranges showed their pale stone through the Clock Tower Courtyard's walls in flickering blocks); world/hlod_build.coplanar_overlaps finds them, test_hlod and the export refuse them.",
